# Practical No. 2(B): Using JSX Syntax in React

## Aim
To use JSX syntax to create a React user interface.

## Source Code

### 1. `src/App.js`

```jsx
import React from "react";
import JSXDemo from "./components/JSXDemo";

function App() {
  return <JSXDemo />;
}

export default App;
```

### 2. `src/components/JSXDemo.jsx`

```jsx
import React from "react";

function JSXDemo() {
  const name = "Sanika Dhanawade";
  const course = "React JS";

  return (
    <div>
      <h2>Student Details</h2>
      <p>Name: {name}</p>
      <p>Course: {course}</p>
    </div>
  );
}

export default JSXDemo;
```

## Output

```text
Student Details

Name: Sanika Dhanawade
Course: React JS
```

## Result
Successfully created a React user interface using JSX syntax and displayed student details using JavaScript variables inside JSX expressions.
